{"w":2400,"lines":[{"y":0.044897556357407553,"h":0.010495584620463405,"t":"C 1718867188","x":0.77155884499256389,"w":0.070051034291585323,"c":0.5},{"w":0.29012346903483077,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","y":0.097383720794351092,"x":0.1008230390430009,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"y":0.1307420492044381,"h":0.01751376490149259,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","w":0.77160491943359366,"x":0.10288066770875398},{"w":0.1604938252766927,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.10082304604020877,"y":0.14811542989978521,"c":1,"t":"Passage 3 below."},{"y":0.18732418952099006,"t":"Insight or evolution?","x":0.34739424592992718,"w":0.29091400146484381,"h":0.02563237750768943,"c":1},{"t":"Two scientists consider the origins of discoveries and other innovative behavior","y":0.22965116263148877,"x":0.11728396275590455,"w":0.75308639526367183,"h":0.017441860778592999,"c":1},{"w":0.7345679219563801,"x":0.10082303480370286,"y":0.26442873984824378,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"Scientific discovery is popularly believed to result from the sheer genius of such intellectual","c":1},{"c":1,"t":"stars as naturalist Charles Darwin and theoretical physicist Albert Einstein. Our view of such","x":0.10082304203834393,"y":0.28052325566746183,"w":0.74279836018880208,"h":0.016002068109591039},{"x":0.10076031233318181,"y":0.29594341568065796,"w":0.76143366495768239,"c":1,"t":"unique contributions to science often disregards the person's prior experience and the efforts of","h":0.018742186722682463},{"w":0.74085118611653644,"y":0.31232691452345551,"t":"their lesser-known predecessors. Conventional wisdom also places great weight on insight in","c":1,"h":0.019423788090898064,"x":0.10076503424007323},{"x":0.10082305754084729,"c":1,"t":"promoting breakthrough scientific achievements, as if ideas spontaneously pop into someone's","y":0.32979976451465076,"h":0.017667844522968212,"w":0.75308639526367194},{"c":1,"y":0.34738372077386659,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"head - fully formed and functional.","w":0.28600822448730467,"x":0.10082304807217497},{"y":0.38074204924589372,"t":"There may be some limited truth to this view. However, we believe that it largely misrepresents","w":0.75514404296874993,"x":0.10288065329648598,"h":0.013250883392226243,"c":1},{"x":0.10288065330060799,"y":0.39680232544826533,"h":0.014563987898180697,"w":0.75514404296874993,"c":1,"t":"the real nature of scientific discovery, as well as that of creativity and innovation in many other"},{"y":0.4142441859337137,"w":0.21810699462890626,"x":0.10082304577490608,"h":0.011627907185728703,"t":"realms of human endeavor.","c":1},{"w":0.74279836018880208,"c":1,"t":"Setting aside such greats as Darwin and Einstein - whose monumental contributions are duly","y":0.44611307429755298,"x":0.10288065264736854,"h":0.01472320376914027},{"c":1,"t":"celebrated - we suggest that innovation is more a process of trial and error, where two steps","x":0.10288065706212099,"w":0.73045267740885411,"y":0.46366279056459558,"h":0.014546867815428799},{"w":0.74485595703124996,"h":0.014534882858869502,"c":1,"x":0.10082306078478619,"t":"forward may sometimes come with one step back, as well as one or more steps to the right or","y":0.47965116297947996},{"h":0.013250883392226243,"w":0.75514404296875004,"x":0.10082304014113939,"y":0.49705535917907229,"t":"left. This evolutionary view of human innovation undermines the notion of creative genius and","c":1},{"t":"recognizes the cumulative nature of scientific progress.","w":0.4423868306477865,"x":0.10082304546580455,"y":0.51295641950775417,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1},{"x":0.10082303480223308,"t":"Consider one unheralded scientist: John Nicholson, a mathematical physicist working in the","c":1,"w":0.73456792195638021,"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.54651162776101592},{"w":0.75514404296875004,"x":0.10082304133455504,"y":0.560954063860852,"t":"1910s who postulated the existence of 'proto-elements' in outer space. By combining different","c":1,"h":0.017667844522968212},{"t":"numbers of weights of these proto-elements' atoms, Nicholson could recover the weights of all","x":0.1007087967987665,"y":0.57518637351718949,"c":1,"w":0.75538798014322917,"h":0.02256038697223639},{"y":0.59593023241190046,"w":0.77777776082356775,"t":"the elements in the then-known periodic table. These successes are all the more noteworthy given","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"x":0.098765440485520148},{"y":0.61189634850770946,"c":1,"h":0.014557139191105239,"t":"the fact that Nicholson was wrong about the presence of proto-elements: they do not actually","x":0.10082306186513383,"w":0.74074071248372397},{"c":1,"t":"exist. Yet, amid his often fanciful theories and wild speculations, Nicholson also proposed a novel","x":0.10074726379246451,"y":0.62669244815999703,"w":0.77998901367187501,"h":0.019563850160201124},{"x":0.098765439571162586,"w":0.78395060221354174,"h":0.016017476296396715,"c":1,"y":0.64534883706263158,"t":"theory about the structure of atoms. Niels Bohr, the Nobel prize-winning father of modern atomic"},{"w":0.74074076334635408,"t":"theory, jumped off from this interesting idea to conceive his now-famous model of the atom.","x":0.098765420681718966,"c":1,"y":0.66279069752821995,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"h":0.013250883392226132,"x":0.10493825925735033,"y":0.69611307392885313,"c":1,"t":"What are we to make of this story? One might simply conclude that science is a collective and","w":0.74691360473632806},{"w":0.73868311564127609,"y":0.71220930217904954,"x":0.1008230511538622,"t":"cumulative enterprise. That may be true, but there may be a deeper insight to be gleaned. We","h":0.016000356213644928,"c":1},{"t":"propose that science is constantly evolving, much as species of animals do. In biological systems,","w":0.77777776082356764,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.72819767428505899,"x":0.10288066680463061},{"y":0.74558303881470478,"x":0.10288065769854086,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"t":"organisms may display new characteristics that result from random genetic mutations. In the same","w":0.78189300537109374},{"w":0.75322001139322925,"c":1,"y":0.76016293029017601,"x":0.10075298504440022,"t":"way, random, arbitrary or accidental mutations of ideas may help pave the way for advances in","h":0.01921367532934537},{"y":0.77906976729555399,"w":0.74691360473632817,"h":0.015988372380376759,"t":"science. If mutations prove beneficial, then the animal or the scientific theory will continue to","c":1,"x":0.10082303292294759},{"t":"thrive and perhaps reproduce.","y":0.79473411681962758,"w":0.23892901102701822,"h":0.015554154579153545,"x":0.10274956713662078,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.86773255796252025,"t":"45","x":0.8580246914705375,"w":0.024691357612609877},{"c":1,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.30612678527832038,"x":0.66991655033568553,"h":0.03375352650564889,"y":0.95314993796778535}],"h":3395}